Hessian:

min sum f_i(x)
s.t. lb <= g(x) <= ub

where some lb and ub are equal


Our lagrangian will have the form:

L(x, nu, mu) = sum f_i(x) + sum_j mu_j*(lb_j - g_j(x)) - sum_j nu_j*(g_j(x) - ub_j)

hessian L(x, nu, mu) = sum D2 f_i(x) - sum_j mu_j D2 g_j(x) - sum_j nu_j * D2 g_j(x)
hessian L(x, lam) = sum D2 f_i(x) + sum_j lam_j D2 g_j(x)

hessian L(x, lam) = sum lam_j D2 h_j(x)
hessian L(x, lam) = sum lam_j L_j(D2 h_j(x_j))


1) Compute dense hessian D2 h_j(x_j) elementwise for a constraint set
2) Copy the weighted dense hessians into the correct locations of the hessian

3) Detect if a hessian is always zero, and don't compute it

